<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0" />
    <title>Cat FAQ</title>
    <style>
      :root {
        --bg: #f5f7fb;
        --panel: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.88);
        --panel-border: rgba(15, 23, 42, 0.08);
        --text: #0f172a;
        --muted: #475569;
        --accent: #7c3aed;
        --accent-soft: rgba(124, 58, 237, 0.12);
        --shadow: 0 24px 60px rgba(15, 23, 42, 0.12);
        --radius: 22px;
      }

      * {
        box-sizing: border-box;
      }

      body {
        margin: 0;
        min-height: 100vh;
        font-family: Inter, ui-sans-serif, system-ui, -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, "Segoe UI", sans-serif;
        color: var(--text);
        background:
          radial-gradient(circle at top left, rgba(124, 58, 237, 0.12), transparent 28%),
          radial-gradient(circle at top right, rgba(14, 165, 233, 0.16), transparent 24%),
          linear-gradient(180deg, #fbfcff 0%, var(--bg) 100%);
        display: grid;
        place-items: center;
        padding: 40px 20px;
      }

      .page {
        width: min(920px, 100%);
      }

      .hero {
        text-align: center;
        margin-bottom: 28px;
      }

      .eyebrow {
        display: inline-flex;
        align-items: center;
        gap: 8px;
        padding: 8px 14px;
        border-radius: 999px;
        background: var(--accent-soft);
        color: var(--accent);
        font-size: 0.85rem;
        font-weight: 700;
        letter-spacing: 0.02em;
        margin-bottom: 18px;
      }

      h1 {
        margin: 0;
        font-size: clamp(2.5rem, 5vw, 4rem);
        line-height: 1;
        letter-spacing: -0.04em;
      }

      .hero p {
        width: min(640px, 100%);
        margin: 16px auto 0;
        font-size: 1.05rem;
        line-height: 1.7;
        color: var(--muted);
      }

      .faq-shell {
        background: var(--panel);
        border: 1px solid var(--panel-border);
        border-radius: 32px;
        box-shadow: var(--shadow);
        backdrop-filter: blur(18px);
        padding: 18px;
      }

      .example + .example {
        margin-top: 14px;
      }

      .example {
        border: 1px solid rgba(15, 23, 42, 0.08);
        border-radius: var(--radius);
        background: linear-gradient(180deg, rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.96), rgba(248, 250, 252, 0.92));
        overflow: hidden;
        transition: transform 180ms ease, box-shadow 180ms ease, border-color 180ms ease;
      }

      .example:hover {
        transform: translateY(-1px);
        border-color: rgba(124, 58, 237, 0.18);
        box-shadow: 0 14px 30px rgba(15, 23, 42, 0.08);
      }

      .question {
        width: 100%;
        border: 0;
        background: transparent;
        padding: 22px 24px;
        display: flex;
        align-items: center;
        justify-content: space-between;
        gap: 18px;
        text-align: left;
        color: inherit;
        cursor: pointer;
        font: inherit;
      }

      .question span:first-child {
        font-size: 1.05rem;
        font-weight: 700;
        line-height: 1.4;
      }

      .icon {
        width: 36px;
        height: 36px;
        border-radius: 50%;
        background: rgba(148, 163, 184, 0.12);
        color: var(--accent);
        display: inline-grid;
        place-items: center;
        flex-shrink: 0;
        transition: background-color 180ms ease, transform 180ms ease;
      }

      .question[aria-expanded="true"] .icon {
        background: var(--accent-soft);
        transform: rotate(45deg);
      }

      .icon::before {
        content: "+";
        font-size: 1.4rem;
        line-height: 1;
        font-weight: 400;
      }

      .details {
        padding: 0 24px 22px;
        color: var(--muted);
        line-height: 1.75;
        font-size: 0.98rem;
      }

      .details p {
        margin: 0;
      }

      .details[hidden] {
        display: none;
      }

      @media (max-width: 640px) {
        body {
          padding: 24px 14px;
        }

        .faq-shell {
          padding: 14px;
          border-radius: 24px;
        }

        .question,
        .details {
          padding-left: 18px;
          padding-right: 18px;
        }

        .question {
          padding-top: 18px;
          padding-bottom: 18px;
        }

        .details {
          padding-bottom: 18px;
        }
      }
    </style>
  </head>
  <body>
    <main class="page">
      <header class="hero">
        <div class="eyebrow">Cat Care Essentials</div>
        <h1>Frequently asked questions about cats</h1>
        <p>
          A clean, quick guide for curious cat people. Tap any question to reveal the answer and learn more
          about behavior, care, and daily life with cats.
        </p>
      </header>

      <section class="faq-shell" aria-label="Cat frequently asked questions">
        <div class="example">
          <button class="question" type="button" aria-expanded="false">
            <span>Why do cats purr?</span>
            <span class="icon" aria-hidden="true"></span>
          </button>
          <div class="details" hidden>
            <p>
              Cats often purr when they feel relaxed and safe, but they may also purr when they want comfort,
              attention, or reassurance. It can signal contentment, self-soothing, or even a response to stress.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="example">
          <button class="question" type="button" aria-expanded="false">
            <span>How often should I feed my cat?</span>
            <span class="icon" aria-hidden="true"></span>
          </button>
          <div class="details" hidden>
            <p>
              Most adult cats do well with two measured meals a day, while kittens usually need more frequent
              feeding. The right schedule depends on age, activity level, and your veterinarian&apos;s guidance.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="example">
          <button class="question" type="button" aria-expanded="false">
            <span>Do indoor cats need playtime?</span>
            <span class="icon" aria-hidden="true"></span>
          </button>
          <div class="details" hidden>
            <p>
              Yes. Indoor cats benefit from daily play that mimics stalking, chasing, and pouncing. Regular
              enrichment helps reduce boredom, supports exercise, and can prevent unwanted behaviors.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="example">
          <button class="question" type="button" aria-expanded="false">
            <span>Why does my cat knead blankets or laps?</span>
            <span class="icon" aria-hidden="true"></span>
          </button>
          <div class="details" hidden>
            <p>
              Kneading is a common behavior that starts in kittenhood and often carries into adulthood. Many
              cats knead when they feel cozy, secure, or affectionate, especially on soft surfaces.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="example">
          <button class="question" type="button" aria-expanded="false">
            <span>What should every cat home include?</span>
            <span class="icon" aria-hidden="true"></span>
          </button>
          <div class="details" hidden>
            <p>
              A comfortable cat setup should include fresh water, a clean litter box, scratching surfaces,
              hiding spots, elevated resting areas, and toys. These basics support both physical health and a
              sense of safety.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>
    </main>

    <script>
      const questions = document.querySelectorAll(".question");

      questions.forEach((button) => {
        button.addEventListener("click", () => {
          const details = button.nextElementSibling;
          const isExpanded = button.getAttribute("aria-expanded") === "true";

          button.setAttribute("aria-expanded", String(!isExpanded));
          details.hidden = isExpanded;
        });
      });
    </script>
  </body>
</html>
